# .npmignore — the anti-re-leak denylist for `npm publish` (2026-07-11 incident).
# The `files` whitelist ships data/ .thetacog/ docs/ so the demo is self-contained; THIS denies the
# private subset within them so the tarball can never carry it again. Mirror of the mirror-to-public
# denylist. Guarded by tests/ops/npm-pack-no-leak.test.mjs (npm pack must show ZERO private paths).

# ── LICENCE PRIVATE KEYS — NEVER publish (2026-08-25) ──
# The package's `files` whitelist does not currently list .thetacog/pmu/licenses/, so npm pack
# is clean today (measured: 1280 files, zero key paths). That is a property of the WHITELIST,
# not a decision about keys — add ".thetacog/" to `files` for any reason and the keyring ships
# with it. Denied here so the answer does not depend on that. An npm tarball is immutable and
# world-readable the moment it publishes; unpublishing does not un-download it.
.thetacog/pmu/licenses/
thetadriven-licence-*.json
*.priv.pem
*.seed

# ── private telemetry / strategy / personal — NEVER publish ──
.thetacog/cache/
.thetacog/pmu/measurements/
.thetacog/pmu/measure-history/
.thetacog/comms/
.thetacog/blog-mail/
data/pmu/shortlex-children-candidate.json
data/pmu/measure-history.ndjson
data/pmu/measure-history.attestation.json
data/pmu/pipeline/
data/pmu/sigma-localize/
data/pmu/study/
docs/comms/
docs/strategy/
docs/outreach/
docs/research/

# build artifacts / deps
node_modules/
# pmu-rust/target/ — DELIBERATELY NOT DENIED HERE, and the reason is load-bearing (bf-5141, 2026-09-07).
#   This line used to read `pmu-rust/target/`. It never did anything: npm's `files` whitelist takes
#   precedence over .npmignore, and `files` lists "pmu-rust/" wholesale, so the denial was
#   structurally unreachable. Every published tarball has in fact shipped target/release/ — on
#   purpose, because target/release/pmu-onchip is the compiled walker a stranger runs with no Rust
#   toolchain. So the old line was doubly wrong: inert, AND it described a policy the package
#   contradicts. The real ban is one subtree (target/debug/) and it lives where npm will honour it:
#   `"!pmu-rust/target/debug"` in package.json "files". Guard: tests/ops/npm-pack-no-debug-build.test.mjs.
*.log
.env
.env.*
.DS_Store
